# Every merge to platform-oss main requires explicit approval from a code
# owner. Combined with branch protection's `require_code_owner_reviews: true`
# and `required_approving_review_count: 1`, this means: no PR reaches main
# without a deliberate approval click.
#
# Rationale: this repo publishes infrastructure packages (mobile-crypto,
# web-crypto, logging) consumed by Loomantix product apps and any external
# OSS users. A merged-but-malicious commit here flows into downstream
# install pipelines via npm, with provenance that traces back to this
# workflow run — i.e., the supply chain trusts these merges. Requiring an
# explicit per-PR approval is the cheapest defense against subtle
# weaponization until the structural mitigations (signed releases, maybe
# a multi-reviewer rule on `packages/**`) land.
#
# CODEOWNERS syntax: https://docs.github.com/repositories/managing-your-repositories-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

